# installed.  It is deliberately absent from p5/payload/filemap and from
# p5-install's map -- a file under /etc/p5 would collide with the installer's
# own namespace refusal (IN-16, p5/contract/paths:229-232).
#
# Every file under $BOND_DIR (= /etc/p5, deploy/p5/bond-xctl:37) gets ONE row
# here, with a WRITER, its READERS, a STATED DEFAULT for when it is absent, and
# a DISPOSITION.  deploy/p5/test-facts.sh sweeps the tree and refuses any
# reference that has no row (UNDECLARED), any row nobody reads (ORPHAN), and any
# cite that no longer resolves (STALE-CITE).  The bar is MECHANICAL: it greps,
# it does not read this prose.  A hand-written list is what U124 invalidated --
# it moved bond-xctl's 1000+ lines into lib/ and every `bond-xctl:NNN` cite on
# the U133 ROADMAP row died silently.
#
# ROW FORMAT   name|kind|root|writer|readers|default|disposition
#
#   kind      control   = a person's INTENT, set through a CLI/UI verb
#             operator  = a person's MEASURED declaration; no CLI today, and
#                         that is legal ONLY because the row says so
#             derived   = the reconciler computes it every tick
#             secret    = install-time material
#             subtree   = a DIRECTORY under the fact root, not a fact
#             forbidden = a fact name that exists only as a REJECTED design
#   root      /etc/p5 for every real P5 fact.  /etc/bond means a STALE root
#             (pre-ADR-005) and is reported as a named ROOT-MISMATCH waiver.
#   writer    `path:line ...`   a real writer
#             OPERATOR          declared operator-written: legal, no CLI
#             NONE              no writer: a COUNTED escalation waiver, and the
#                               disposition MUST start with ESCALATED:
#   readers   `path:line ...`, or NONE (only with an UNBUILT: disposition)
#   default   what happens when the file is ABSENT, then `@` and the cite that
#             ESTABLISHES it.  Measured from code, never asserted.
#
# CITE FORM   path:line          -- the line must still contain the fact name
#             path:line~TOKEN    -- the line must contain TOKEN instead.  Used
#                                   where the write is through the portal's
#                                   catalogue-bounded dynamic key ($_k), which
#                                   never spells the fact name.
#
# NOT SWEPT, and stated here rather than hidden in a regex:
#   * names beginning with `.` are write temps (.agg_env.new,
#     deploy/p5/lib/xctl-actions.sh:151), not facts.
#   * $BOND_DIR/$k, /$_k, /$key are the portal's dynamic key
#     (deploy/p5/portal/cgi/p5-portal:137,333,347).  They are resolved through
#     the catalogue that bounds them, deploy/p5/portal/catalogue/fields; a
#     catalogue key with no row here is a FAIL.
#   * harness writes (orchestration/ecosim/**, deploy/p5/bond-accept) are NOT
#     writers.  bond-accept is P5's on-box acceptance runner
#     (deploy/p5/bond-accept:1-9).  Counting it would let `mode` look like it
#     had a writer on paths that do not ship.
#
# THE $BOND_DIR SPELLING AND THE LITERAL SPELLING ARE ONE FACT, ONE ROW.  agg_env is
# the row that proves the checker greps both spellings: it is referenced ONLY as
# the literal /etc/p5/agg_env at deploy/p5/init.d/bond-agg:22,28.
#
